{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And if the tzara'at breaks out and covers all the skin of the nega</b> — Now, the breaking out is not a sign of purity until it breaks out over the entire body, excluding the places that the Sages specified in the Mishnah (Negaim 8:5), which do not prevent the one who has turned entirely white. If so, what is the meaning of \"all the skin of the nega\"? Rather, its meaning is: \"and the tzara'at covered all the skin of the nega\" — from his head to his feet, that is, it says that the place of the nega turned white along with the entire body. This teaches that if the entire body turned white but the appearance of the nega reverted to bohak or healed — he is impure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:23.863781425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}